findings

  FINDING a 5 ms frame carries 81 byte packets at 129.7 kbps effective against the 128 kbps asked for

what must not be zero

  PASS  packets came out of the encoder          2000
        every percentile and the effective rate in this run is computed over these packets, so a run that produced none makes each of those figures an absence rather than a number
  PASS  the decoded channels stay distinct       1
        two channels reading one frequency is consistent with a fold to mono, with one channel encoded twice, and with a detector measuring its own scratch buffer, and a frame count is consistent with all three

what must be zero

  PASS  every submitted frame came back          0 over 480000 frames_submitted
        Opus is lossy in amplitude and exact in length, so a decoded length that disagrees with the submitted one is a defect and not a tolerance; the population is the submitted frames, because two counts of nothing agree perfectly

what else must hold

  PASS  encode p99 under a tenth of the frame    56 against a bound of 500
        a tenth of the 5 ms frame is 500 us, and an encoder under that cannot be the term that matters in a budget measured in whole milliseconds; p99 rather than the mean, because a frame late once every hundred is a click a listener hears
  PASS  the left channel decodes to its own tone 997 against 997 give or take 5
        a byte count and a frame count agree just as happily when the decoder returns silence, and this project has read that agreement as success; 997 Hz comes out of the decoded samples, at a window resolution of 2 Hz
  PASS  the right channel decodes to its own tone 1996.998 against 1997 give or take 5
        the two channels carry different frequencies so that channel order is provable rather than assumed, and a right channel reading 997 Hz is what a swap looks like

PASS 6 of 6 checks hold and every declared subsystem was exercised

